# Design System

## Colors
- Use ONLY CSS custom properties from `globals.css`. Never hardcode hex values.
- Available tokens: `--color-cream`, `--color-cream-dark`, `--color-parchment`, `--color-terracotta`, `--color-terracotta-light`, `--color-terracotta-dark`, `--color-sage`, `--color-sage-light`, `--color-muted-gold`, `--color-dusty-blue`, `--color-warm-gray`, `--color-soft-brown`
- For project card colors: use values from `PALETTE_COLORS` in `src/lib/constants.ts`
- **No red-family colors anywhere** (`#FF...`, `#E5...`, `#DC...` ranges). Errors use amber/terracotta. Destructive confirmations use terracotta, not red.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div style={{ color: '#C67B5C' }}>

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="text-terracotta">
// or
<div style={{ color: 'var(--color-terracotta)' }}>
```

## Typography
- **Caveat**: accent text only — section headers, empty states, special labels
- **Inter**: all body text, form labels, buttons, inputs, captions
- Never mix fonts within a single UI element

## Animations
- Enter: 200–300ms ease-out
- Exit: 150ms ease-in
- No transitions under 150ms for content changes

## Accessibility
- All interactive elements need visible focus rings: `focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-terracotta-light`
- Color is never the sole state indicator — always pair with an icon or text label
- Every form input must have an associated `<label>`, not just a placeholder
